Title: Signal Fires
Author: ClearCut Demo
Draft date: August 31, 2026

EXT. GRIFFITH OBSERVATORY - PRE-DAWN

Fog presses against the hill while a documentary crew unloads two Asteron field cameras.

MAYA ORTIZ
We have nine minutes before the city wakes up.

JONAH REED
Then we make every frame count.

CUT TO:

INT. MOBILE PRODUCTION VAN - PRE-DAWN

Maya pins a reproduction of The Great Wave off Kanagawa above the monitor wall.

MAYA ORTIZ
The sponsor wants the red bottle silhouette in every setup.

Jonah turns a contour bottle away from camera and lowers the radio playing Blue Monday.

INT ABANDONED RADIO STATION - NIGHT

A handwritten note on the console reads, Ask Ada Lovelace what the machine remembers.

EXT. HARBOR CHECKPOINT - MORNING

A prop officer lifts a seven-point Northstar badge as the van rolls beneath the inspection lights.

OFFICER VALE
Credentials and filming permit.

JONAH REED
Both are in the blue folder.

INT. COMMUNITY CLINIC - DAY

DR. LENORA SHAW closes a chart before the lens can catch the patient number.

DR. SHAW
Her relapse began after she left East Mercer, room 214.

Maya quietly marks the line for review.

EXT. BOARDWALK MURAL - SUNSET

The crew frames a newly painted bicycle mural while its artist watches from across the rail.

MURAL ARTIST
You asked to film the wall, not to sell my work.

MAYA ORTIZ
Then the camera stays down until we agree.

INT. PROJECTION BOOTH - NIGHT

A faded Glass House poster curls above the projector. Jonah threads the final reel.

JONAH REED
Here's looking at you, kid.

Maya stops the projector before the borrowed line reaches the theater speakers.

DISSOLVE TO:

EXT. ROOFTOP - DAWN

The skyline brightens behind an unbranded camera and a blank canvas.

MAYA ORTIZ
No borrowed light this time.

Jonah starts recording as the first clean frame fills the monitor.

FADE TO BLACK.
